+# Lobu enterprise operational ontology evaluation
+
+## Purpose
+Demonstrate Lobu as a practical operational ontology platform to an external enterprise architect. This is a self-contained synthetic commerce scenario, **not** a claim of Palantir feature parity or a production certification.
+
+## Principles
+- Use Lobu-native entity schemas, typed links, identities, source-backed entities, events, SQL views, Automations, approvals, agents and SDK as code. Reuse built-in UI and workspace-specific overrides before creating bespoke UI.
+- Keep the enterprise evaluator's environment isolated. No Trendyol/Alibaba customer data, account connections, names, internal architecture or credentials.
+- Every asserted fact has a source and time; an inference is visibly different from an observation. Corrections and retractions must not erase history.
+- Tests must be reproducible on a clean workspace, idempotent on rerun and independently inspectable by an external agent.
+- No claim of enterprise readiness until authorization, failure recovery, observability, isolation, upgrade and concurrency gates pass.
+
+## Domain scenario
+Marketplace Seller -> Product -> Listing -> SKU -> Warehouse -> InventoryPosition -> Order -> OrderLine -> Shipment -> Payment -> Return -> Refund.
+Contextual seller, buyer, merchant-of-record and carrier roles are distinct from party identity.
+Cross-system evidence: marketplace order feed, warehouse stock updates, shipping events and payment ledger (all synthetic).
+
+## Demonstration flows
+1. Install from code into fresh workspace; inspect types, relationships, views, events and Automation definitions.
+2. Ingest conflicting inventory updates from independent sources; preserve both and explain accepted availability.
+3. Seller changes listing price; enforce field ownership, approval and audit.
+4. New order reserves stock; deterministic Automation derives availability and fulfillment eligibility.
+5. LLM Automation interprets a synthetic supplier email; proposes, rather than silently executes, a change.
+6. Shipment delayed; trigger alert and show evidence, source revision and linked affected orders.
+7. Return and refund; demonstrate process state transitions and idempotent retries.
+8. Correct an older source record after a newer update; prove stale output cannot become current.
+9. Withdraw one of two independent supporting claims; prove remaining support survives.
+10. External read-only agent audits model and data; cross-organization reads/writes are denied.
+
+## Required test gates
+- Domain: typed endpoints, identity reconciliation, temporal qualifications, graph traversal, query correctness, no silent conflicts.
+- Event/Automation: duplicate delivery, retries, out-of-order completion, independent retraction, deterministic and LLM runs, exact provenance.
+- Governance: human approval, field ownership, roles, access to private source evidence, tenant isolation.
+- Platform: fresh install, restart/recovery, version upgrade, performance under skew, clear logs/metrics, reproducible deployment.
+- UX: native pages, views, component overrides, agent discovery, no custom browser replacing native Lobu collections.
+
+## Status
+This file defines acceptance criteria. The existing FIBO catalog and synthetic financial demo are a separate working prototype; they do not satisfy these enterprise gates.
